sequenceDiagram
  autonumber

  actor EX as External clinician<br/>(GP / home nurse)
  participant POR as External clinician portal<br/>(Pathway Orchestrator UI)
  participant BFF as Professional BFF
  participant ITM as itsme
  participant EHE as eHealth federation
  participant IDB as Identity broker
  participant AME as Access Management Engine
  participant TRI as Transmural integration layer
  participant CORE as Core service
  participant BUS as Event bus
  participant EHRI as EHR integration layer
  participant HIX as Chipsoft HiX

  Note over EX,HIX: External clinician (no HiX account) authenticates via eHealth federation +<br/>itsme. Access is scoped to patients with whom they have a documented<br/>therapeutic relationship, episode-bounded, audit-logged.

  EX->>POR: Open external portal URL<br/>(or click invite link from email)
  POR->>BFF: GET /session
  BFF-->>POR: 401 → redirect to login

  POR->>EHE: SAML/OIDC federation request<br/>scope=openid profile RIZIV<br/>+ care-relationship attribute
  EHE->>ITM: Strong-auth via itsme<br/>(eID/passkey fallback)
  ITM-->>EHE: User authenticated<br/>(RIZIV number, INSS)

  EHE->>EHE: Resolve therapeutic relationships<br/>(eHealth attribute service)
  EHE-->>POR: SAML assertion / OIDC token<br/>{RIZIV, INSS, role=physician,<br/>care_relationships=[patient_INSS_1,2,3]}

  POR->>BFF: POST /auth/callback<br/>(federation token)
  BFF->>IDB: Validate token<br/>(eHealth issuer signature)
  IDB-->>BFF: Validated claims

  BFF->>AME: Resolve external entitlements<br/>{RIZIV, claimed_patients}
  AME->>TRI: Verify therapeutic relationship<br/>per patient<br/>(eHealth attribute confirmation)
  TRI->>EHE: GET TherapeuticRelationship<br/>(eHealth API)
  EHE-->>TRI: Active relationships<br/>+ episode windows
  TRI-->>AME: Confirmed scope:<br/>patient IDs + episode windows

  AME->>CORE: Lookup patients by INSS<br/>(internal API)
  CORE-->>AME: Platform patient IDs<br/>+ active pathways

  AME-->>BFF: Active role = External clinician<br/>+ episode-bound entitlements<br/>(per-patient, per-window)
  BFF-->>POR: Session token<br/>+ scoped patient list

  POR-->>EX: Render scoped patient list<br/>(only patients in confirmed relationship)

  %% --- In-session actions ---
  EX->>POR: Open patient pathway
  POR->>BFF: GET pathway state<br/>(scoped by entitlement)
  BFF->>AME: Authorise — episode check<br/>(is the episode still open?)
  AME-->>BFF: Authorised<br/>(episode window valid)
  BFF->>CORE: GET pathway state
  CORE-->>BFF: Pathway timeline<br/>(shielding policy applied —<br/>some items hidden from external roles)
  BFF-->>POR: Render pathway view

  EX->>POR: Upload referral document<br/>(e.g. home-nursing assessment)
  POR->>BFF: POST document
  BFF->>AME: Authorise upload<br/>(scope check)
  AME-->>BFF: Authorised
  BFF->>CORE: POST document<br/>+ link to pathway + patient
  CORE->>BUS: Emit DocumentUploaded event

  par Surface to ZAS clinician
    BUS->>EHRI: Write DocumentReference to HiX
    EHRI->>HIX: POST DocumentReference<br/>(FHIR R4, with external author)
    HIX-->>EHRI: Doc ID
    BUS->>EHRI: Create Task in HiX worklist<br/>"External clinician contributed"
    EHRI->>HIX: POST Task
  and Audit
    BUS->>EHRI: Provenance — external action<br/>{RIZIV, INSS-relationship, timestamp}
    EHRI->>HIX: POST Provenance
  end

  %% --- Episode end ---
  Note over EX,HIX: When the patient's episode ends (pathway complete or relationship<br/>withdrawn in eHealth), entitlement expires.

  CORE->>BUS: Emit EpisodeEnded event
  BUS->>AME: Revoke external entitlement<br/>for this patient
  AME->>AME: Remove from external user's scope<br/>(server-side, immediate effect)

  EX->>POR: Attempt to open patient (later)
  POR->>BFF: GET pathway state
  BFF->>AME: Authorise
  AME-->>BFF: Denied (episode ended)
  BFF-->>POR: 403 forbidden
  POR-->>EX: "This patient is no longer in your<br/>active care scope. Contact ZAS<br/>if access is still needed."

  Note over EX,HIX: External clinicians never receive HiX credentials.<br/>The eHealth federation + AME together enforce that they see only<br/>the patients they are entitled to, only during the active episode.